  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1114 AM MDT Fri Aug 7 2026\n\nUpper high currently near the Four Corners region and will not\nmove much over the next 4-5 days. The moisture will be moving in\nand out during this time. Looking at WV, there is still decent\nmoisture located over southern NM with drier air sitting in\nnorthern NM into CO which will start moving in for Sat, especially\nover eastern CWA. This evening looks similar to yesterday with\nstorms moving NE to SW with gusty winds, small hail and brief\nheavy rain. The 12Z GFS came in drier this evening but then brings\nan area of rain through the region between about 03Z-09Z. Looking\nat ensembles, the SREF and GEFS also in support of this, so I did\nkeep some low PoPs going through this time. Overnight lows look \nsimilar to last night with low to mid 70s common. \n\nFor Sat, the drier air starts to push in from the NNE. May get a\nfew storms near the Sacs and then a storm or 2 on the lowlands,\nbut the Gila still looks like the best area with scattered\ncoverage. High temperatures will be warming back up to near 100\nfor the lowlands. Drier air continues to push in Sat night, so any\nprecip will be ending by sunset. The drier air will allow lows to\ndrop a few more degrees compared to recent days. \n\nMon and Tue look to be mirrors of Sun with the focus for any\nstorms being in the Gila region with just a couple isolated storms\nin the Sacs while the lowlands remain dry. The drier low level air\nwill help temperatures warm up to the upper 90s to around 105\nduring this time. If any Heat Advisories are needed, it will\nremain over the lower RGV.  \n\nGoing into late next week, the upper high will finally start to\nshift into a more favorable monsoonal position off to the east and\nwe setup a nice deep ESE flow bringing in Gulf moisture and\nincreased storm chances areawide. Temperatures will also struggle\nto get above 100 degrees.",
